From 95a5042e4b51a7c06e576d8095a48923de1b203a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:29:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 93/98] pvr: zero the unused words of render target descriptors

pvr_arch_init_mrt_desc() set intermediate_size and the used valid_mask
words only, so priority and the other valid_mask words kept whatever was in
memory. priority decides which render targets get output registers, and
the descriptor is part of the load op program cache key, so equal render
setups never matched and every dynamic render recompiled its load op
program.

Zeroing the descriptor fixes 6 CTS cases that failed before
(renderpass{1,2} attachment.8.797 and attachment_allocation.shrink.66) and
removes the per-render shader compile.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_mrt.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_mrt.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_mrt.c
index 3971d64..89f2286 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_mrt.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_mrt.c
@@ -88,6 +88,11 @@ void pvr_arch_init_mrt_desc(VkFormat format, struct usc_mrt_desc *desc)
     * register
     */
    const uint32_t part_bits = 0;
+
+   /* Unused valid_mask words and the priority are part of the load op cache
+    * key, so they must not be left uninitialised.
+    */
+   memset(desc, 0, sizeof(*desc));
    if (vk_format_is_color(format) &&
        pvr_arch_get_pbe_accum_format(format) == PVR_PBE_ACCUM_FORMAT_INVALID) {
       /* The VkFormat is not supported as a color attachment so `0`.
